{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting, design, mass and bulk, would disrupt the surrounding pattern of development as a discordant addition and would be at odds with the character of the surrounding dwellings. It therefore fails to represent a high quality design, and would have a detrimental impact on the character and appearance of the surrounding area, as well as to the local distinctiveness of the Becontree Estate, a non-designated heritage asset. The proposal thus fails to comply with the following policies which seek to ensure development proposals are sympathetic to local character and appearance and preserve or enhance the local distinctiveness and historic character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023)Policies D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies CP2 and CP3 of the Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010)Policy BP11 of the Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development fails to provide clarity that additional demand for parking could be adequately accommodated by the proposed motorbike provision. No details surrounding the access of the existing dropped kerb for both properties has been provided, and the applicant has not demonstrated that the crossover can be accessed interchangeably and independently from each property. It has not been clarified that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. Officers are unable to determine whether the proposal would result in parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BR9 of the Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policy DMT2 of The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)"
  ],
